# Freyalise's Winds and a stun counter both replace the untap of a permanent that has both counters (CR 122.1d, 614.1a), and
# the permanent's controller chooses which applies (CR 616.1e); the other then no longer applies, as the event is no untap
# any more (CR 614.6, 616.1f). Bot1's Rapier Wit taps Bot2's Ornithopter on Bot1's turn and stuns it, and the tap gives it a
# wind counter. In Bot2's untap step on turn four Bot2 applies the Winds first: every wind counter comes off and the stun
# counter stays. On turn six the stun counter alone replaces the untap.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Freyalise's Winds
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Rapier Wit
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Freyalise's Winds.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rapier Wit.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Wind = 1
Bot2.Replace(wind counters)
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Wind = (absent)
[T6 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Wind = (absent)
